%I A402374 #6 Nov 24 2026 18:01:18
%S A402374 0,0,0,3,16,56,210,653,1929,5241
%N A402374 Number of Frobenius pseudoprimes with respect to the Fibonacci polynomial x^2 - x - 1 (A212424) less than 10^n.
%C A402374 An odd composite number m not divisible by 5 is such a pseudoprime if x^m == x (mod m, x^2 - x - 1) when m == +-1 (mod 5), or x^m == 1 - x (mod m, x^2 - x - 1) when m == +-2 (mod 5). Since x^m == F(m)*x + F(m-1) (mod x^2 - x - 1), where F = A000045, these conditions read F(m) == 1 and F(m-1) == 0 (mod m), or F(m) == -1 and F(m-1) == 1 (mod m), respectively.
%C A402374 The terms a(1)-a(10) were obtained by testing every odd m < 10^10 not divisible by 5; the pseudoprimes found coincide with the terms of A212424 below 10^10.
%C A402374 The tables of Dana Jacobsen (see link) give a(11) = 14149, a(12) = 37527 and a(13) = 98702.
%H A402374 Dana Jacobsen, <a href="https://ntheory.org/pseudoprimes.html">Pseudoprime Statistics, Tables, and Data</a>.
%e A402374 a(4) = 3 because the Frobenius pseudoprimes below 10^4 are 4181, 5777 and 6721.
%o A402374 (PARI) isfrob(m) = if(m<2 || isprime(m) || gcd(m, 10)>1, return(0)); my(M=Mod([1, 1; 1, 0], m)^m, k=kronecker(5, m)); if(k==1, M[2, 2]==0 && M[1, 2]==1, M[2, 2]==1 && M[1, 2]==-1);
%o A402374 a(n) = sum(m=1, 10^n, isfrob(m));
%Y A402374 Cf. A000045, A055550, A081264, A212423, A212424, A319168.
%K A402374 nonn,more,new
%O A402374 1,4
%A A402374 _Patryk Majda_, Nov 17 2026
